# The style the rest of this family of projects uses -- CPU-Power, simple-login-gui and the
# rations-amp editor all share it, and src/gfx/ and src/platform/ are vendored from them.
#
# IT CHANGED WHEN Qt WENT. The previous style here was Allman braces at two spaces, which was
# this project's own; keeping it would have meant reformatting every vendored file on import and
# losing the ability to diff canvas.cpp or x11window.cpp against the copy it came from. That diff
# is worth more than the old brace placement.
#
# The two bridge .c files are deliberately NOT formatted to this: they are untouched, working
# audio code, and rewrapping four thousand lines of it to settle a brace argument would bury
# every real change that ever lands near them.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
ColumnLimit: 100
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
PointerAlignment: Right
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
SortIncludes: false
IndentCaseLabels: true
AccessModifierOffset: -4
